From a921f8fb03fc970bc657fe60dbd0d7d71df8a66e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 13:04:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/23] gated_delta_net : rewrite chunked phase A, 293us ->
 210us per launch

The phase A kernel (gdn_chunk_prepare) was latency-bound: ~165 dynamic
barriers and 512 scalar global loads per thread in the k_cumsum and
attn_causal stages.

- closure: 16x16-block forward substitution (146 syncs) replaced by an
  exact 4x4-blocked substitution over the whole 64x64 (16 syncs). The
  4x4 diagonal blocks have nilpotency index 4, so D(i,i) = I + A + A^2 +
  A^3 is exact; the off-diagonal blocks D(i,j) = D(i,i) @ (A(i,j) D(j,j)
  + sum A(i,k) D(k,j)) follow in row passes. A(i,k) is read from a
  preserved smem copy (s_A, packed strictly-lower) because the in-place
  row-pass writes would clobber it. Level 0 solves the 4x4 blocks in
  registers via shuffles.
- decay cumsum: Hillis-Steele (13 syncs) replaced by a warp-shuffle scan
  (2 syncs); the chunk's k rows are prefetched into registers during it.
- k_cumsum/k_cumdecay and attn_causal: v[j][v0..v0+7] and q rows are read
  as float4 (falling back to scalars when the stride/base is unaligned),
  cutting 512 scalar global loads per thread to 128.

47/47 GATED_DELTA_NET tests, PPL 6.2677 (within error bars of 6.2426),
generation matches. Phase A 276.5 -> ~210 us/launch (6.63 -> ~5.1 ms per
pp512); bench noise makes the pp512 delta hard to pin, expected +2%.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet
